      <Concept PreferredConceptYN="Y">
        <ConceptUI>M0000842</ConceptUI>
        <ConceptName>
          <String>Alzheimer Disease</String>
        </ConceptName>
        <ScopeNote>A degenerative disease of the BRAIN characterized by the insidious onset of DEMENTIA. Impairment of MEMORY, judgment, attention span, and problem solving skills are followed by severe APRAXIAS and a global loss of cognitive abilities. The condition primarily occurs after age 60, and is marked pathologically by severe cortical atrophy and the triad of SENILE PLAQUES; NEUROFIBRILLARY TANGLES; and NEUROPIL THREADS. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp1049-57)
        </ScopeNote>
